HTB — Follow The Money
Category	Difficulty	Platform	Date compiled
OSINT (blockchain forensics)	Easy	Hack The Box	March 2026
Skills demonstrated: blockchain transaction tracing, address clustering, mixer detection, exchange-KYC attribution, tool chaining across a provided analytics environment.

Summary:
The scenario is a cryptocurrency-fraud investigation: trace funds from a seized Bitcoin wallet, de-anonymize the suspect, and answer six evidence questions. 
The HTB lab provides an in-browser investigation environment with commercial-grade analytics tools, so the work is done inside that environment rather than with external scripts.
Each answer unlocks the context for the next, following the standard money-trail progression: cluster the addresses, quantify the fraud, detect obfuscation, then pivot from on-chain data to the suspect's real-world identity and location via exchange KYC records.

The lab's browser gives access to:
Crystal Analytics	Network graphing and address clustering; identifies the funding exchange
OXT Advanced	Transaction-pattern analysis; CoinJoin / mixing detection
Chainalysis KYT	Know-Your-Transaction attribution; links the address to registration data
Arkham Intelligence	Entity and metadata resolution; geographic / temporal data

All are reached from the challenge portal; no external setup is required.

